{"pageProps": {"params": {"versionId": "59", "usfm": "LUK.21.NIV"}, "audioVersionInfo": {"title": "ESV Hear the Word Audio Bible", "copyright_long": {"text": "English: ESV Audio Old and New Testament", "html": "English: ESV Audio Old and New Testament"}, "copyright_short": {"text": "\u2117 2016 Crossway", "html": "<p>\u2117 2016 Crossway</p>"}, "version_id": 59, "id": 1, "publisher_link": "", "dramatized": false, "publisher": {"id": 575, "name": "Hear Book Audio", "local_name": "Hear Book Audio", "url": null, "description": null}}, "type": "chapter", "chapterInfo": {"audioChapterInfo": [{"download_urls": {"format_mp3_32k": "//audio-bible-cdn.youversionapi.com/1/32k/LUK/21-0a976aa00f4aaeee4902622a611d4784.mp3?version_id=59", "format_hls": "//audio-hls.youversionapi.com/1/m4a/32k/LUK/21-0a976aa00f4aaeee4902622a611d4784.m3u8?version_id=59"}, "id": 1, "version_id": 59, "title": "ESV Hear the Word Audio Bible", "timing_available": true, "dramatized": false, "default": true}, {"download_urls": {"format_mp3_32k": "//audio-bible-cdn.youversionapi.com/1668/32k/LUK/21-29a0ee706a941791b3391d44aa9a6c88.mp3?version_id=59", "format_hls": "//audio-hls.youversionapi.com/1668/m4a/32k/LUK/21-29a0ee706a941791b3391d44aa9a6c88.m3u8?version_id=59"}, "id": 1668, "version_id": 59, "title": "Living Water Bible - ESV Music Project by Lutheran Bible Translators", "timing_available": false, "dramatized": true, "default": false}], "content": "<div class=\"version vid59 iso6393eng\" data-vid=\"59\" data-iso6393=\"eng\">\n    <div class=\"book bkLUK\">\n        <div class=\"chapter ch21\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21\">\n            <div class=\"label\">21</div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">The Widow&#8217;s Offering</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"verse v1\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.1\"><span class=\"label\">1</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    For ver. 1-4, see Mark 12:41-44   </span></span><span class=\"content\">Jesus</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">21:1 </span><span class=\"ft\">Greek </span><span class=\"fq\">He</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> looked up and saw the rich </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">2 Kgs. 12:9 </span></span><span class=\"content\">putting their gifts into </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">John 8:20 (Gk.)</span></span><span class=\"content\">the offering box, </span></span><span class=\"verse v2\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.2\"><span class=\"label\">2</span><span class=\"content\">and he saw a poor widow put in two </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 12:59</span></span><span class=\"content\">small copper coins.</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">21:2 </span><span class=\"ft\">Greek </span><span class=\"fq\">two lepta</span><span class=\"ft\">; a </span><span class=\"fq\">lepton </span><span class=\"ft\">was a Jewish bronze or copper coin worth about 1/128 of a </span><span class=\"fq\">denarius </span><span class=\"ft\">(which was a day&#8217;s wage for a laborer)</span></span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.3\"><span class=\"label\">3</span><span class=\"content\">And he said, </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;Truly, I tell you, </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[2 Cor. 8:2, 12]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">this poor widow has put in more than all of them.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v4\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.4\"><span class=\"label\">4</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">For they all contributed out of their abundance, but she out of her </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Phil. 4:11] </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">poverty put in all </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 8:43</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">she had to live on.&#8221;</span></span></span></div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">Jesus Foretells Destruction of the Temple</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v4\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.4\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v5\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.5\"><span class=\"label\">5</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    For ver. 5-36, see Matt. 24:1-51; Mark 13:1-37  </span></span><span class=\"content\">And while some were speaking of the temple, how it was adorned with noble stones and offerings, he said, </span></span><span class=\"verse v6\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.6\"><span class=\"label\">6</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;As for these things that you see, </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 19:43, 44; See ch. 17:22</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">the days will come when there will not be left here one stone upon another that will not be thrown down.&#8221;</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v7\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.7\"><span class=\"label\">7</span><span class=\"content\">And they asked him, &#8220;Teacher, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Acts 1:6, 7]</span></span><span class=\"content\">when will these things be, and what will be the sign when these things are about to take place?&#8221; </span></span><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.8\"><span class=\"label\">8</span><span class=\"content\">And he said, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Jer. 29:8; Eph. 5:6; Col. 2:8; 2 Thess. 2:3; 1 John 3:7 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;See that you are not led astray. For </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Jer. 14:14; 1 John 2:18 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">many will come in my name, saying, </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See John 8:24 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8216;I am he!&#8217; and, </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Matt. 3:2; 4:17; Mark 1:15]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8216;The time is at hand!&#8217; Do not go after them.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v9\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.9\"><span class=\"label\">9</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">And when you hear of wars and tumults, do not be </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 24:37 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">terrified, for these things </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Rev. 1:1</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">must first take place, but the end will not be at once.&#8221;</span></span></span></div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">Jesus Foretells Wars and Persecution</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v9\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.9\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v10\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.10\"><span class=\"label\">10</span><span class=\"content\">Then he said to them, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">2 Chr. 15:6; [Rev. 6:4] </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;Nation will rise against nation, and </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Isa. 19:2</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">kingdom against kingdom.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v11\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.11\"><span class=\"label\">11</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">There will be great </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Rev. 6:12 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">earthquakes, and in various places </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Acts 11:28; Rev. 6:8 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">famines and pestilences. And there will be </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Isa. 19:17 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">terrors and great </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 11:16; Matt. 16:1; Mark 8:11; [ver. 25; Rev. 12:1, 3; 13:13; 15:1]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">signs from heaven.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v12\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.12\"><span class=\"label\">12</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">But before all this </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">For ver. 12-17, [Matt. 10:17-22] </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">they will lay their hands on you and persecute you, delivering you up to </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Acts 22:19; 26:11 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">the synagogues and </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Acts 4:3; 5:18; 8:3; 12:4; 16:24; 24:27; 2 Cor. 11:23 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">prisons, and you </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Acts 16:19 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">will be brought before </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Acts 27:24] </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">kings and </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Acts 17:6; 18:12; 24:1; 25:6</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">governors for my name&#8217;s sake.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v13\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.13\"><span class=\"label\">13</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Phil. 1:13, 14, 19]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">This will be your opportunity to bear witness.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v14\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.14\"><span class=\"label\">14</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">Settle it therefore in your minds </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 12:11</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">not to meditate beforehand how to answer,</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v15\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.15\"><span class=\"label\">15</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">for </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Ex. 4:12; Jer. 1:9] </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">I will give you a mouth and </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Acts 6:10 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">wisdom, which none of your adversaries will be able to withstand or </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Acts 4:14]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">contradict.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.16\"><span class=\"label\">16</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">You will be delivered up </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ch. 12:53; Matt. 10:35]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">even by parents and brothers</span></span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">21:16 </span><span class=\"ft\">Or </span><span class=\"fq\">parents and brothers and sisters</span></span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">and relatives and friends, and some of you they will put to death.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v17\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.17\"><span class=\"label\">17</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">John 15:18-21; [ch. 6:22]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">You will be hated by all for my name&#8217;s sake.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v18\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.18\"><span class=\"label\">18</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">But </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ver. 16; John 10:28]; See 1 Sam. 14:45</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">not a hair of your head will perish.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v19\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.19\"><span class=\"label\">19</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">By your </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Rom. 5:3; [Matt. 10:22; 24:13]; See Heb. 10:36</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">endurance you will gain your lives.</span></span></span></div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">Jesus Foretells Destruction of Jerusalem</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v19\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.19\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v20\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.20\"><span class=\"label\">20</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;But </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    See ch. 19:43   </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">when you see Jerusalem surrounded by armies, then know that </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Dan. 9:27\n        </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">its desolation has come near.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v21\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.21\"><span class=\"label\">21</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">Then let those who are in Judea flee to the mountains, and let those who are inside the city depart, and let not those who are out in the country enter it,</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v22\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.22\"><span class=\"label\">22</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">for these are </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Isa. 34:8; 63:4; Hos. 9:7 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">days of </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ch. 18:7, 8] </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">vengeance, to fulfill </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Matt. 1:22</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">all that is written.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v23\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.23\"><span class=\"label\">23</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 23:29 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">Alas for women who are pregnant and for those who are nursing infants in those days! For there will be great distress upon the earth and </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">1 Thess. 2:16</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">wrath against this people.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v24\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.24\"><span class=\"label\">24</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">They will fall by the edge of the sword and </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Deut. 28:64] </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">be led captive among all nations, and </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Rev. 11:2; [Ps. 79:1; Isa. 63:3, 18; Dan. 8:13; Zech. 12:3] </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">Jerusalem will be trampled underfoot by the Gentiles, </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Dan. 12:7; Rom. 11:25]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">until the times of the Gentiles are fulfilled.</span></span></span></div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">The Coming of the Son of Man</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v24\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.24\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v25\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.25\"><span class=\"label\">25</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;And </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Isa. 13:10; 24:23; Ezek. 32:7; Joel 2:10, 31; 3:15; Acts 2:20; [Amos 5:20; 8:9; Zeph. 1:15; Rev. 6:12; 8:12]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">there will be signs in sun and moon </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Rev. 6:13; [Isa. 14:12; 34:4]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">and stars, and on the earth </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    [Ps. 65:7]  </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">distress of nations in perplexity because of the roaring of the sea and the waves,</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v26\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.26\"><span class=\"label\">26</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">people fainting with fear and with foreboding of what is coming on the world. For </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Isa. 34:4]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">the powers of the heavens will be shaken.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v27\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.27\"><span class=\"label\">27</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">And then they will see </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Dan. 7:13 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">the Son of Man coming in a cloud </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Matt. 26:64; Mark 9:1; [Matt. 25:31]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">with power and great glory.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v28\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.28\"><span class=\"label\">28</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">Now when these things begin to take place, straighten up and </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Job 10:15 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">raise your heads, because </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Rom. 8:23; Eph. 4:30; [Rom. 13:11]; See ch. 1:68</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">your redemption is drawing near.&#8221;</span></span></span></div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">The Lesson of the Fig Tree</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v28\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.28\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v29\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.29\"><span class=\"label\">29</span><span class=\"content\">And he told them a parable: </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;Look at the fig tree, and all the trees.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v30\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.30\"><span class=\"label\">30</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">As soon as they come out in leaf, you see </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 12:57; [Matt. 16:3]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">for yourselves and know that the summer is already near.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v31\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.31\"><span class=\"label\">31</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">So also, when you see these things taking place, you know that the kingdom of God is near.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v32\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.32\"><span class=\"label\">32</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See ch. 9:27</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">Truly, I say to you, this generation will not pass away until all has taken place.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v33\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.33\"><span class=\"label\">33</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 102:26; Isa. 51:6; 2 Pet. 3:10; [Matt. 5:18; Heb. 12:27] </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">Heaven and earth will pass away, but </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 119:89; Isa. 40:8; 1 Pet. 1:23, 25</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">my words will not pass away.</span></span></span></div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">Watch Yourselves</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v33\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.33\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v34\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.34\"><span class=\"label\">34</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;But watch yourselves </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    [Rom. 13:13; 1 Thess. 5:6, 7; 1 Pet. 4:7]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">lest </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        James 5:5   </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">your hearts be weighed down with dissipation and drunkenness and </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    [Matt. 13:22]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">cares of this life, and </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        1 Thess. 5:3, 4; [ch. 12:40]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">that day come upon you suddenly </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Eccles. 9:12; Isa. 24:17  </span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">like a trap.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v35\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.35\"><span class=\"label\">35</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">For it will come upon all who dwell on the face of the whole earth.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v36\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.36\"><span class=\"label\">36</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">But </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 12:37; Matt. 25:13; 26:41; Mark 14:34-38; Acts 20:31; 1 Cor. 16:13; 1 Thess. 5:6; 1 Pet. 5:8 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">stay awake at all times, </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See ch. 18:1 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">praying that you may </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Hos. 12:4] </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">have strength to escape all these things that are going to take place, and </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Rev. 6:17</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">to stand before the Son of Man.&#8221;</span></span></span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v36\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.36\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v37\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.37\"><span class=\"label\">37</span><span class=\"content\">And </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Matt. 26:55 </span></span><span class=\"content\">every day he was teaching in the temple, but </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 22:39; Matt. 21:17; Mark 11:19; [John 8:1; 18:2] </span></span><span class=\"content\">at night he went out and lodged on </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Matt. 21:1</span></span><span class=\"content\">the mount called Olivet. </span></span><span class=\"verse v38\" data-usfm=\"LUK.21.38\"><span class=\"label\">38</span><span class=\"content\">And early in the morning </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 37 above]</span></span><span class=\"content\">all the people came to him in the temple to hear him.</span></span></div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</div>", "copyright": {"html": "<p>The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers.</p>", "text": "The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers."}, "next": {"canonical": true, "usfm": ["LUK.22"], "human": "Luke 22", "toc": true, "version_id": 59}, "previous": {"canonical": true, "usfm": ["LUK.20"], "human": "Luke 20", "toc": true, "version_id": 59}, "reference": {"usfm": ["LUK.21"], "human": "Luke 21", "version_id": 59}}, "usfm": "LUK.21.NIV", "locale": "en", "versionData": {"audio": true, "copyright_short": {"html": "<p>The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers.</p>", "text": "The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publis